<article class="env-lemma" id="024B">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/024B">Lemma <span data-tag="024B">85.27.4</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $\pi : Y \to (X/S)_\bullet $ be a cartesian morphism of simplicial schemes. Set $V = Y_0$ considered as a scheme over $X$. The morphisms $d^1_0, d^1_1 : Y_1 \to Y_0$ and the morphism $\pi _1 : Y_1 \to X \times _ S X$ induce isomorphisms </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ V \times _ S X &  &  Y_1 \ar[ll]_-{(d^1_1, \text{pr}_1 \circ \pi _1)} \ar[rr]^-{(\text{pr}_0 \circ \pi _1, d^1_0)} &  &  X \times _ S V. }  \]
</div>
  <p> Denote $\varphi : V \times _ S X \to X \times _ S V$ the resulting isomorphism. Then the pair $(V, \varphi )$ is a descent datum relative to $X \to S$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of (part of) Lemma <a href="/tag/07TC" data-tag="07TC">85.27.2</a> as the displayed equation of that lemma is equivalent to the cocycle condition of Descent, Definition <a href="/tag/023V" data-tag="023V">35.34.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>